<!-- SUBSCRIBE -->
<section class="subscribe-section">
  <div class="subscribe-inner">
    <p class="subscribe-heading">Get my essays as they're published</p>
    <form data-members-form class="subscribe-form">
      <input type="email" placeholder="Enter your email" class="subscribe-input" data-members-email required>
      <button type="submit" class="subscribe-btn">Subscribe</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- DEEP DIVES -->
<section class="deep-dives-section">
  <div class="section-label">Deep Dives</div>
  <div class="deep-dive-header">
    <h3>Fine-Tuning VLAs at Scale</h3>
    <span class="deep-dive-subtitle">A 5-Part Series on Physical AI</span>
  </div>
  <div class="deep-dive-grid">
    <div class="deep-dive-intro">
      <p>VLAs go straight from camera input to motor control. One model, no perception stack, no hand-coded planner. But the training infrastructure that worked for LLMs doesn't transfer.</p>
      <p>This series covers what's different and what to build - from data pipelines through evaluation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="deep-dive-parts">
      <a href="#" class="deep-dive-part"><span class="part-num">1</span><span class="part-title">The Data Problem</span><span class="part-hint">Heterogeneous data breaks standard pipelines</span></a>
      <a href="#" class="deep-dive-part"><span class="part-num">2</span><span class="part-title">Decoupling CPU and GPU Scaling</span><span class="part-hint">Why vertical scaling makes it worse</span></a>
      <a href="#" class="deep-dive-part"><span class="part-num">3</span><span class="part-title">Distributed Data Loading</span><span class="part-hint">Streaming, sharding, and shuffle strategies</span></a>
      <a href="#" class="deep-dive-part"><span class="part-num">4</span><span class="part-title">Training Loop Optimization</span><span class="part-hint">Profiling before you guess</span></a>
      <a href="#" class="deep-dive-part"><span class="part-num">5</span><span class="part-title">Evaluation at Scale</span><span class="part-hint">Offline metrics vs real-world performance</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

